    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Max agrees to help behind the restaurant bar and marvels at the computerized cash register. When Nastya comes in to order two espressos, she is surprised to see a cook posing as the new bartender. Listen to their playful exchange in Russian first, and then we will review it in English.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Так вот как выглядит эта система.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я думал, это просто касса.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сделай два эспрессо, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что ты тут делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "А я теперь новый бармен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да ладно тебе выдумывать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тебя на кухне видела.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты же повар.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "У меня очень много талантов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "А в душе я бармен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя уже починил аппарат?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Конечно, всё прекрасно работает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее вари кофе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Сию секунду. Всё будет готово.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's review this funny encounter behind the bar line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Так вот как выглядит эта система.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So this is what this system looks like.' Max inspects the computerized cash register at the bar.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я думал, это просто касса.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I thought it was just a cash register.' Max chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'thought' for the ongoing action, followed by 'simply' and 'cash register'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сделай два эспрессо, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Make two espressos, please.' Nastya arrives at the bar with a beverage order.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что ты тут делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you doing here?' Surprised to find a kitchen helper standing behind the bar counter.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "А я теперь новый бармен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I am now the new bartender.' Max confidently invents a new position for himself.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да ладно тебе выдумывать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, stop making things up.' Here Nastya anchors the line on the word meaning 'all right' and builds the thought around 'to make up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тебя на кухне видела.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I saw you in the kitchen.' The phrasing opens with 'kitchen' before bringing in 'saw' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты же повар.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are a cook after all.' Nastya delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'cook'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "У меня очень много талантов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have very many talents.' Max uses the classic Russian possession phrasing — literally 'at me' rather than a verb meaning 'to have', combining 'very' with 'many' and 'talents'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "А в душе я бармен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And at heart I am a bartender.' A poetic Russian idiom meaning deep down inside his soul.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя уже починил аппарат?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did Kostya already fix the machine?' Nastya turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'already', pairing it with 'fixed' and 'machine'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Конечно, всё прекрасно работает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course, everything works wonderfully.' Max expresses this naturally by combining the word for 'of course' with 'wonderfully' and 'works'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее вари кофе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then make coffee faster.' Nastya leads with the direct command form meaning 'brew', pairing it with 'then' and 'faster'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Сию секунду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Right away.' An idiom literally meaning 'this very second'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Всё будет готово.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything will be ready.' Max chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'will be' for the ongoing action, followed by 'ready'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
